The `owner` and `name` variables, derived from `repo_slug`, are directly interpolated into a GraphQL query string. This is vulnerable to GraphQL injection if `repo_slug` contains double quotes. An attacker could potentially manipulate the GraphQL query to perform unauthorized actions or exfiltrate data, depending on the permissions of the GitHub token used. It is recommended to use GraphQL variables instead of string interpolation.

```suggestion
	pinned_json=$(gh api graphql -F owner="$owner" -F name="$name" -f query="
		query(\$owner: String!, \$name: String!) {
			repository(owner: \$owner, name: \$name) {
				pinnedIssues(first: 10) {
					nodes {
						issue {
							id
							number
							state
							title
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}" 2>>"$LOGFILE" || echo "")
```

