![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using a type assertion `as { data: Uint8Array }` is brittle. If `NOSTR_BOT_NSEC` contains a different type of NIP-19 encoded string (e.g., an `npub`), `nip19.decode` will return an object with a different structure, but the type assertion will suppress compile-time errors, leading to a runtime failure when `getPublicKey` is called with invalid data. It's safer to check the `type` property of the decoded object to ensure it's an `nsec` key before accessing its data.

```suggestion
const decoded = nip19.decode(botNsec);
if (decoded.type !== 'nsec') throw new Error('Invalid NOSTR_BOT_NSEC: not an nsec key.');
const sk = decoded.data;
const pk = getPublicKey(sk);
```

